Subject: [PATCH] Ticketing System, Blogs module, rating->scoring fix,
 suspension gate, 5-job limit (Part A verify + Part B1/B3/B5)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Part A re-verification fixes:
- Post a Job now enforces the spec's 5-simultaneous-active-jobs limit
  per client, with a clear message when the limit is hit (was entirely
  unenforced before).
- Fixed a real data-modeling gap: the current user's own Pilot rating
  (used in scoring, suspension, and job cancellation penalties) was
  three disconnected hardcoded 4.7 values across bid.tsx,
  professional.tsx, and track.tsx — none of which fed into each other.
  Consolidated onto a single CURRENT_USER.providerRating field that
  calculateProviderScore, the professional-info screen, and the
  cancellation flow all now read/write consistently.

Part B1 — Ratings & Review System:
- Completing a job (client Approves) now genuinely applies +0.1 to the
  provider's rating, capped at 5.0.
- Provider cancellation now applies -0.5 to CURRENT_USER.providerRating
  specifically (not an unrelated BID_PROVIDERS entry, which was the
  previous bug), and sets a real providerSuspendedUntil timestamp.
- New SuspensionGate component: renders a full-screen, non-dismissible
  suspension notice (28-day countdown) in place of the entire provider
  dashboard when the rating check trips — not just an alert popup as
  before. Client-side access remains available with a 'Switch to
  Client View' escape hatch, per spec.

Part B3 — Ticketing System:
- Ticket type + data store with mock-incrementing IDs in the exact
  SB-TKT-YYYY-NNNNNN format.
- Raise a Ticket flow: category selection (all 8 spec categories) ->
  detail form with optional photo attachments -> submission with a
  generated ticket ID shown to the user.
- My Tickets list (status badges: Open/In Review/Waiting/Resolved/
  Closed) and a full ticket detail screen with a status stepper —
  no delete action exists anywhere, view-only per spec.
- The Dispute path in the Review screen now auto-generates a real
  ticket (job ID, category, date, amount pre-filled) instead of just
  showing a generic 'ticket created' message.
- 'Get Help' button added to completed/approved/closed jobs in the
  tracking screen, routing into Raise a Ticket pre-linked to that job.

Part B5 — Blogs:
- Full mock content: 6 posts across all required categories with
  real multi-paragraph body text (not placeholder lorem ipsum).
- Blog Listing screen: search, category pills, featured carousel.
- Blog Detail screen: hero image, full body, native Share sheet,
  Related Articles (same category).
- Compact 'From the Blog' teaser added to Home (3-card horizontal
  row) without disrupting existing Dashboard sections, plus a Blog
  entry point from the Profile menu.

Full workspace typecheck: zero errors.

Not covered in this pass (follow-up): Notifications System extension
(per-screen bell badge audit, non-dismissible critical notifications,
full trigger simulation for every listed event), FAQs re-verification
against the newer category list, and the remaining Part A2/A3 items
(job edit before/after tracking, bid-disappears-on-selection).
